        "original_id": "54e46807-8b48-5a32-8c78-049099bbbb52",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Music groups: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters, Queen\n- Songs: \"Everyday America\", \"Heaven for Everyone\"\n- Places: Atlanta\n- Events: 2005 Planet Rock poll\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- In 2005, Roger Taylor was voted the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock history by radio listeners in a Planet Rock poll.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- Taylor Hawkins of Foo Fighters acclaimed Roger Taylor as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver wrote the song \"Everyday America\".\n- Roger Taylor wrote the song \"Heaven for Everyone\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
